      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "You can visually inspect the serpentine belt for cracks, fraying, or glazing, which indicates wear. To check for looseness, try gently wiggling the belt around the pulleys; excessive play suggests it needs adjustment or replacement. If it appears intact but still squeals, a pulley bearing might be failing, which would require professional diagnosis.",
