    {
      "role": "user",
      "content": "ok that makes sense. i checked it and noticed some small cracks on the underside. it also seems to happen more when it's raining or humid outside. is there any other reason why an engine might just suddenly start acting up with these weird noises even if the parts look mostly okay?",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
    {
      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "The humidity or rain might exacerbate a slight belt issue, but other components can cause noise even if the belt looks decent. Failing tensioner pulleys develop noise because their internal bearings seize up, which can mimic belt problems. Additionally, worn-out accessory bearings, like those on the alternator or pump, can produce squealing sounds that are mistaken for belt issues.",
      "source": "target",
